    "result_text": "All done. The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year begins 1 July), changing behaviour as specified.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`model/Owner.java`):\n- Added `FISCAL_YEAR_START_MONTH = 7` and a `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` helper that returns the four-digit fiscal year, labelled by the calendar year it *ends* in (a date on/after 1 July belongs to the next year's FY).\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` returning `'FY<YY>'` derived from the (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`, null when unset.\n- `getMembershipNumber()` now derives the `-M<YY>` segment from the **fiscal year** rather than the calendar registration year.\n- `getMembershipPoints()` now awards the tenure points based on **elapsed fiscal years** (`>= MEMBERSHIP_TENURE_FISCAL_YEARS`, i.e. at least one FY boundary crossed) instead of a 365-day window; removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import and `MEMBERSHIP_TENURE_DAYS`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: added the read-only `fiscalYear` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field/setter), and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to match the new fiscal-year semantics.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**: added an `@AfterMapping addFiscalYear(...)` populating the DTO from `Owner.getFiscalYear()`, and updated the `membershipNumber` javadoc.\n\nThe acceptance test (`fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) passes; with today's date (2026-09-30 \u2192 FY2027), the owner correctly gets `fiscalYear=FY27` and `membershipNumber=...-M27`.\n\nNote on a convention choice I had to make: the spec says `FY<YY>` without pinning whether the two digits are the fiscal year's *start* or *end* year. I used the common finance/AU convention of labelling by the ending year (1 Jul 2026\u201330 Jun 2027 \u2192 `FY27`). If you'd prefer the start-year label (`FY26`), it's a one-line change in `fiscalYearOf`.\n\nNo commit was made since this isn't a git repository \u2014 let me know if you'd like me to initialize one.",
